{"title":"2022 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae0734db2c961f41d5627f830ea0e5c1de76262f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{Z}\\to\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> be a function such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d0e714dd3855ef2e740b789ae984e1d7cd5f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a5b9594b5af4a2ad26c6a7c0d6447075ca86d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(|x^2-4|)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"21\" /> whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c9cbf3e3c04dc46dea71f60acd0cb704eabc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />. Suppose further that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24d83651f34ac0c6bf4c1c0f0fdaffcde458028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f(x+1)-f(x)|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14e1fc2610d0ab9747b552684df1356df224e62a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of possible sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63ce779c6a2e8d99b0999f097761a71f0ac0e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{f(1),f(2),\\dots,f(21)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. In cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/34648cd9e715095b52fa0c4bebb70e3267ea8dae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAD}=60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/309aebbf56e055c13eb597b52577c4bacd5d1f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=CD=T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer. Find the median of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6a00ed49999d60e66be68752dee9e26cd17cc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial of degree 10, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef23fa2ea2baca6509e5deca6f5cf1a46b3735f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i)=i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/153f75bfa224812cb73354ce39824a7e1e658567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,\\dots,10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b97c43049af0eaf96ab79da507ea2fd35a6acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(11) =T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821e2e2bd3b98506d6a01b9cb7c0d47ffed7f6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_3_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 3 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017160511\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 111/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4124/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24539:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017160511 and revision id 280190. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}